<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Why is the sky blue? / 为什么天空是蓝色的？</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="container">
        <!-- English Column -->
        <div class="column" id="english">
            <h2>English</h2>
            <h2>For a 3-Year-Old Toddler</h2>
            <p>Imagine the sunlight is a big box of rainbow colors. When the light reaches the sky, it hits tiny bits of air. The blue color loves to play, so it bounces and bounces all over the sky! That's why when you look up, you see that beautiful blue color dancing everywhere above you.</p>

            <h2>For a High School Teenager</h2>
            <p>The sky is blue because of a phenomenon called Rayleigh scattering. Sunlight looks white, but it's actually made of all the colors of the rainbow. When sunlight enters the Earth's atmosphere, it strikes gas molecules and small particles. Blue light travels in shorter, smaller waves than red light. Because of this, blue light is scattered in all directions more than other colors, which is why our eyes perceive the blue light coming from every part of the sky.</p>

            <h2>For a Physics PhD</h2>
            <p>The blue color of the sky is primarily due to Rayleigh scattering, which occurs when electromagnetic radiation interacts with particles much smaller than the wavelength of the incident light. The scattering intensity $I$ is inversely proportional to the fourth power of the wavelength ($I \propto \lambda^{-4}$). Since blue light has a shorter wavelength than the red end of the spectrum, it is scattered significantly more efficiently by the nitrogen and oxygen molecules in the atmosphere. While violet light is scattered even more, the human eye is much more sensitive to blue, and the solar spectrum has fewer violet photons than blue, resulting in the perceived blue hue of the sky.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Chinese Column -->
        <div class="column" id="chinese">
            <h2>中文版</h2>
            <h2>给3岁的小宝宝</h2>
            <p>想象阳光是一个装满了彩虹颜色的大盒子。当光到达天空时，它撞击了微小的空气颗粒。蓝色喜欢玩耍，所以它在整个空中到处跳来跳去！这就是为什么当你抬头时，你会看到美丽的蓝色在你头顶到处跳舞。</p>

            <h2>给高中生</h2>
            <p>天空之所以是蓝色的，是因为一种瑞利散射（Rayleigh scattering）现象。阳光看起来是白色的，但实际上是由彩虹中的所有颜色组成的。当阳光进入地球大气层时，它会撞击气体分子和小微粒。蓝光的波长比红光更短、更小。正因如此，蓝光在各个方向上的散射比其他颜色剧得多，这就是为什么我们的眼睛感知到来自天空各个部分的蓝光。</p>

            <h2>给物理学博士</h2>
            <p>天空呈现蓝色主要是由于瑞利散射致的，这种散射发生在电磁辐射与远小于入射光波长的粒子发生相互作用时。散射强度 $I$ 与波长的四次方成反比（$I \propto \lambda^{-4}$）。由于蓝光的波长比光谱红端短，大气中的氮气和氧气分子对其散射的效率高得多。虽然紫光的散射程度更高，但人眼对蓝色的敏感得多，而且太阳光谱中的紫光光子少于蓝光光子，导致感知到的天空呈蓝色。</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
